Publish the state information the LiDAR pushes on /diagnostics (diagnostic_msgs/DiagnosticArray)

Base: Livox-SDK/livox_ros_driver2 21445540f0d100dc86a7e6df312dd70bbdb4afdf, with Livox-SDK2 c0796f04 (the pins in
third_party/drivers.repos). setup.sh applies this file with git apply to the copy it builds
(<workspace>_livox/stage/livox_ros_driver2); the checkout is not changed. Gouda: DEC-479, DEC-494.

What it does (ROS 2 only; the ROS 1 build is unchanged):
* registers the SDK2 callback SetLivoxLidarInfoCallback, which the driver did not use. The SDK calls it on its own
  thread with the state push (0x0102) as a JSON string (LivoxLidarStateInfoToJson, parse_lidar_state_info.cpp)
* for each push, publishes one DiagnosticArray on /diagnostics (absolute name, rclcpp default QoS: reliable, volatile,
  keep last 10), header.stamp = the ROS time of receipt, with one status: name "mid360", hardware_id "" (no serial
  number or address), message "info push", level from lidar_diag_status (the worst of its four 4-bit module levels:
  0 OK, 1 WARN, 2 or 3 ERROR, an undefined level above 3 ERROR; STALE when the push has no usable lidar_diag_status)
* values (KeyValue, text) only for these keys, under the SDK's names: cur_work_state, core_temp (0.01 degC, as the
  integer), powerup_cnt, last_sync_time, time_offset, time_sync_type, status_code, lidar_diag_status,
  lidar_flash_status, FW_TYPE, hms_code, version_app, version_loader, version_hardware. Integers in decimal, arrays
  of integers as compact JSON ("[0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0]"), a JSON string as its text. Other keys (sn, mac, product_info, the
  *_ipcfg blocks, ...) are left out, and so is an allowed key with any other value (a fraction, an object, ...)
* the point cloud, IMU and configuration paths of the driver are not changed

Threads: the callback runs on the SDK's command thread. One mutex guards the publisher, clock and logger; Stop()
(first thing in ~DriverNode) clears them under it, so no publish overlaps or follows the node's destruction. The
state is never freed because the SDK has no way to wait for a running callback. Exceptions are caught and logged.
src/call_back/lidar_status_info.h has the parsing and the level, without ROS (test/test_lidar_status_info.cpp).

